        "section_id": "MA-S1",
        "writer_text": "## Motivation: revisit GraphRAG shortcomings from relation extraction errors\n\nGraphRAG systems that rely on pre-extracted relations are vulnerable to error propagation when the extraction step produces incomplete or incorrect edges, degrading downstream retrieval quality. This work revisits that dependency by adopting a graph-structured retrieval formulation that does not require a separate relation extraction stage, thereby eliminating the error source at its origin.",
